<section class="saas-legal-page">
  <div class="saas-container saas-page-shell">
    <div class="saas-page-hero">
      <p class="saas-legal-kicker">Custom Stickers</p>

      <h1>Custom Sticker Maker Online</h1>

      <p>
        Create custom stickers from text prompts or portraits. Use simple descriptions for mascots,
        products, pets, characters, objects, and social sticker ideas.
      </p>
      <a class="saas-button saas-button-primary" href="/#generator">Make a Custom Sticker</a>
    </div>

    <div class="saas-info-grid">
      <article class="saas-info-panel">
        <h2>Prompt to sticker</h2>

        <p>
          Describe the subject, style, mood, and any useful details. Short prompts usually work best
          for clean sticker-ready artwork.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="saas-info-panel">
        <h2>Portrait to sticker</h2>

        <p>
          Upload a portrait when you want a custom avatar, reaction sticker, or character-like
          result from a real face.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="saas-info-panel">
        <h2>Regenerate variations</h2>

        <p>
          Keep useful prompts in history, then regenerate or make variations when you want a new
          pose, expression, or color direction.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>How to make a custom sticker</h2>

      <ol>
        <li>Choose one main subject: a pet, mascot, product, character, object, or portrait.</li>

        <li>
          Add the sticker style: cute, clean, bold outline, white border, simple background.
        </li>

        <li>Describe the mood or action, then generate one sticker or a small prompt batch.</li>

        <li>Use history to retry failed prompts, favorite strong results, and download files.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Custom sticker prompt templates</h2>

      <div class="saas-prompt-list">
        <code>[subject] mascot sticker, [emotion], clean white border, simple background</code>
        <code>[product] as a cute character sticker, friendly face, bright colors</code>
        <code>[pet or portrait] avatar sticker, expressive face, crisp outline</code>
        <code>[object] reaction sticker, playful pose, rounded icon style</code>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Custom sticker use cases</h2>

      <p>
        Use the custom sticker maker for brand mascots, creator avatars, product reaction stickers,
        classroom icons, community badges, social posts, and design experiments. Keep each prompt
        focused so the sticker subject stays easy to recognize.
      </p>

      <p>
        For custom subjects, write the object or character first, then add the sticker job: mascot,
        badge, reaction, avatar, label, thumbnail, or social post accent.
      </p>

      <p>
        Custom sticker prompts work best when they name one subject and one job: mascot, badge,
        reaction, avatar, or social accent. Guests can try 3 custom generations with no sign up
        before buying credits.
      </p>

      <div class="saas-related-links">
        <.link navigate={~p"/ai-sticker-generator"}>AI Sticker Generator</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/sticker-maker-online"}>Sticker Maker Online</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/reaction-sticker-maker"}>Reaction Sticker Maker</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/cute-sticker-ideas"}>Cute Sticker Ideas</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/kawaii-sticker-maker"}>Kawaii Sticker Maker</.link>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="saas-faq">
      <details open>
        <summary>How do I write a custom sticker prompt?</summary>

        <p>
          Start with the subject, then add mood, style, and use case. For example: cheerful coffee
          cup mascot, clean white border, cute reaction sticker, simple background.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Can I make custom sticker batches?</summary>

        <p>
          You can add multiple prompts on separate lines. The history page groups generated
          stickers into batches, shows progress, and supports batch download.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What format should I download?</summary>

        <p>
          PNG is useful for editing and broad compatibility. WebP is smaller for websites and
          social assets. Original keeps the upstream generated format.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
